  "body": "**Link to problem area**:\r\n\r\nhttps://spec.matrix.org/v1.6/#identity, https://spec.matrix.org/v1.6/identity-service-api/, and everywhere.\r\n\r\n**Issue**\r\n\r\nThe names \"identity service\" and \"identity server\" *repeatedly* cause confusion with people thinking they are responsible for managing user identity in Matrix, which is not the case at all.\r\n\r\n(For clarity: all they do is provide a way of mapping from a [\"third-party identifier\"](https://spec.matrix.org/v1.6/appendices/#3pid-types) such as email address or phone number onto a Matrix User ID, to make it easier for your existing contacts to find you.)\r\n\r\nI can't really think of a good name though. \"Third-party identity mapping service\" doesn't exactly trip off the tongue. Suggestions welcome.\r\n",
